Based on the context provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes a JSON schema with the following structure:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "error": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "code": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 409
        },
        "message": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "details": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "resume_token": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "resume_details": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "checkpoint_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "resume_position": {
                  "type": "integer"
                },
                "resume_reason": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The `kv_crc` value inside v2 resume tokens is computed using the CRC32 algorithm. The algorithm takes the binary representation of the key-value pair as input and produces a 32-bit CRC checksum as output. This checksum is then encoded in base64 and included in the resume token as a string.
